 "tagline": "What I know, what I value, what I hope for.",
 "description": "Sort my world by what I experience and know, what I still need to check, what I hold myself to, and what I hope for.",
 "inspiration": "Original: Kant’s three Critiques ask how knowledge is possible and where its limits lie (Pure Reason), how reason can guide action through duty (Practical Reason), and how we judge beauty and purpose in nature (Judgment). He summed up philosophy in four questions: What can I know? What ought I to do? What may I hope? What is a human being?\n\nMinest adaptation: the areas of this template follow those questions in everyday words. It is a modern, Kant-inspired way to sort a personal world; it does not carry out his transcendental philosophy. The twelve categories are kept as an advanced lens, not as twelve folders.",
